    "result_text": "All 34 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule following the codebase's established pattern (derived values are computed and stored on the `Owner` entity at create time, then surfaced through the `OwnerMapper`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `householdSize` field mapped to a new `household_size` column, with getter/setter, alongside the existing derived fields (`namesakeCount`, `bulkSignupWarning`).\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after computing the other derived fields, it now stores the household size on the new owner: `countHouseholdMembers(...) + 1`. The new `countHouseholdMembers` helper counts existing owners sharing the same `householdId` (derived by `Households.householdId` from normalized last name + address), and `+ 1` accounts for the owner being created \u2014 giving the household size *after* this create.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `membershipTier` now returns `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falling back to the existing SILVER (`namesakeCount == 0 && email != null`) and BRONZE rules unchanged.\n\n4. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `household_size INTEGER` column. The test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change is required there; I updated all four for consistency.\n\nThe `Cp23Tests` GOLD test, the `Cp15Tests` SILVER/BRONZE tests, and the full suite (34 tests) all pass.",
